  "summary": "Kernel tests, phenotype rescaling and multi-tissue eQTL or single-cell prioritization all move beyond marginal single-variant association toward gene-level evidence.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is association inference that jointly models heterogeneous variant classes, phenotypes or functional layers rather than relying on marginal single-variant tests. PrediXSKAT embeds PrediXcan-predicted expression into the SKAT kernel, testing rare coding and common cis-regulatory variants together to improve gene-level power. GiMat extends multivariate kernel regression to test SNP gene-gene interactions across multiple dichotomous phenotypes. SIQReg revisits an upstream choice usually left fixed, learning a phenotype scale transformation that minimizes quantile heterogeneity and improves GWAS, TWAS and polygenic prediction in UK Biobank. A second strand targets post-GWAS effector-gene prioritization at type 2 diabetes loci. CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTL PIPs and allelic fold changes across five metabolic tissues. CELL-X combines fine-mapped T2D genes with single-cell islet atlas data in an out-of-memory framework to prioritize beta-cell-relevant genes by cell type and disease state. SIQReg and GiMat are published; the other three remain preprints.",
